---
/**
 * Page-specific (how-it-works): the eval result as a scannable stat block.
 * Two numbers surfaced from prose, the run-it-yourself command kept verbatim.
 * Filled surface, no borders. Scoped CSS, theme-aware via Starlight tokens.
 */
---

<div class="eval">
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="num">9 in 10</span>
      <span class="cap">right note ranked first</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="num">~97%</span>
      <span class="cap">in the top five the assistant reads</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="foot">
    Measured across the two example vaults and 39 everyday questions. A small test, and the number will move. Run it yourself with <code>bun run eval</code>.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .eval {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 10%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
  }
  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .num {
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
  }
  .cap {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .foot {
    margin: 0.95rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .foot code {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-gray-3) 25%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.85rem;
    }
  }
</style>
